<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<scheme version="2.0" title="predictive analytics" description="The regression analysis predicted profit using delivery method, segment, region, category, subcategory, sales, quantity, and discount. Categorical features were encoded using the first category as the reference, and the dataset was divided into 80% training and 20% testing data.&#10;Five-fold cross-validation showed that Gradient Boosting achieved the lowest RMSE of IDR 1.76 million and the highest R² of 0.764, indicating the strongest overall ability to explain profit variation and reduce large prediction errors. The model comparison also favored Gradient Boosting over Random Forest and Linear Regression based on mean squared error. Random Forest recorded the lowest MAE of IDR 331,784.53, while Linear Regression performed the weakest with an R² of 0.304. MAPE was excluded because zero actual-profit values produced infinite results.&#10;On the holdout testing data, Gradient Boosting achieved an improved R² of 0.838 and an RMSE of IDR 1.20 million. It predicted total profit of IDR 819.20 million, compared with the actual IDR 888.81 million, resulting in an underprediction of approximately IDR 69.62 million or 7.83%. Therefore, Gradient Boosting was selected as the primary model, although its output should be treated as an estimate rather than an exact financial result.">
